Ladybird applies an SVG text run’s computed letter-spacing and
word-spacing when shaping it, as Blink, WebKit, and Gecko all do.
Blink sets them on the scaled font LayoutSVGInlineText builds
(SetLetterSpacing() and SetWordSpacing()). WebKit adds them per
character in SVGTextLayoutEngineSpacing::calculateCSSSpacing(). And
Gecko’s ResolveLetterSpacing() and ResolveWordSpacing() in
nsTextFrame.cpp scale them for SVG text by its font-size scale factor.
